From 2dbb6de374646d273d4312d9800de82ff0377f85 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 08:20:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(resume): retry ordinary interrupted turns throughout
 backend lifetime [daveey]

The boot sweep can see a still-live writer, or finish before a later turn is
interrupted. The lifetime observer only considered update-pause/job reasons,
so ordinary interruption markers were never adopted after those races.

Observe every eligible marker and enter the same session.resume admission
path, retaining freshness, attempt-cap, opt-out, writer, code-skew and deletion
guards. Rename the private helpers and migrate their test consumers.

Proof: new ordinary-marker regression fails on baseline (no resume call), then
passes with this fix. Focused startup/restart/observer/queue suites: 153 passed.
Remaining startup-resume consumers: 266 passed. Full scripts/check: 21 checks ok.
Reference implementation: fedbf7d1234616636651b035e532bea88ba1117e (not published).
